            <ArticleTitle>A Sterically Constrained Tricyclic PC3 Phosphine: Coordination Behavior and Insertion of Chalcogen Atoms into P-C Bonds.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>832-835</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1002/anie.201711373</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>A tricyclic phosphine has been generated that has a rigid molecular backbone with the P atoms exclusively bound to C(sp2 ) atoms as well as a very large Tolman angle and buried volume. It is an interesting new ligand in coordination chemistry (Au, Pd complexes) and shows unusual insertion reactions into its endocyclic P-C bonds facilitated by its inherent molecular strain.</AbstractText>
